{"evidence":"Part II, PDF page 33, printed p. 217; The scan has a true bottom footnote, called after triviale; restore it with the existing SourceFootnote macro and retain the anchor. PDF QA amendment: preserve the explicit superscript call 11) as well as the footnote body; SourceFootnote itself emits only the footnote text. The scan places the call after the period following triviale.","new":"\textsuperscript{11)}\SourceFootnote{11}{\LayerTarget{tohoku:footnote:11}
The nontrivial spectral sequence obtained
converges to $\operatorname{Ext}_U(A,B)$, and its initial term is
$H^p\bigl(G,\operatorname{Ext}_O^q(A,B)\bigr)$ ($U$ being the ring generated
by $\mathbf Z(G)$ and the $G$-ring $O$, subject to the commutation relations
$g\lambda g^{-1}=\lambda^g$ for $\lambda\in O$, $g\in G$). Note that this
spectral sequence can be obtained more easily directly, using projective
resolutions of $A$ instead of injective resolutions of $B$. Indeed, it is very
easy to see that if $A$ is a free $U$-module, then $A$ is a free $O$-module
and $\operatorname{Hom}_O(A,B)$ is a $\Gamma^G$-acyclic $G$-module.}

\LayerTarget{tohoku:consequence:edge-homomorphisms-five-term}
The preceding spectral sequences yield edge homomorphisms and five-term exact
sequences, which we shall not write down.
\LayerTarget{tohoku:transition:degeneration-case}
We shall make explicit only one particular case of degeneration:

"}

{"evidence":"Part II, PDF page 37, printed p. 221, bibliography [1]. The enlarged original glyph has its rounded left bowl at x-height and its right stem descending below the baseline. Final-PDF visual review detected that the initial rotated-glyph macro placed the whole letter below the baseline. A primary-rendered comparison confirms that raising the baseline-rotated h by the current x-height reproduces the printed alignment. This changes only glyph placement.","new":"\usepackage{wrapfig}
\usepackage{graphicx}
% Reproduce the inverted h in bibliography entry [1], printed p. 221.
\providecommand{\SourceTurnedH}{%
  \begingroup
  \setbox0=\hbox{x}%
  \raisebox{\ht0}{\rotatebox{180}{h}}%
  \endgroup}"}
